{"total":120,"totalPage":3,"page":2,"pageSize":50,"items":[{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cecd","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3301,"bookHadithIndex":51,"text":"It was narrated that Ibn ‘Umar said:“At the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) we used to eat while walking, and drink while standing up.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3301-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3301-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3301-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3301-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cece","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3302,"bookHadithIndex":52,"text":"It was narrated that Anas said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) like gourd.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3302-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3302-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3302-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3302-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cecf","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3303,"bookHadithIndex":53,"text":"It was narrated that Anas said:“Umm Sulaim sent with me a basket of fresh dates for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), but I did not find him, as he had just gone out to a freed slave of his who had invited him and made food for him. I came to him and he was eating, and he called me to eat with him. He (the freed slave) had served him Tharid with meat and gourd, and he liked the gourd, so I started to collect the (pieces of) gourd and put them near him. When he had eaten he went back to him house and I put the basket (of dates) before him, and he started to eat them and share them, until he finished the last of them.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3303-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3303-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3303-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3303-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced0","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3304,"bookHadithIndex":54,"text":"It was narrated from Hakin bin Jabr that his father said:“I entered upon the Prophet (ﷺ) in his house, and he had some of this gourd. I said: ‘What is this?’ He said: ‘This is Qar’; it is Dubba’. We augment our food with it.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3304-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3304-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3304-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3304-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced1","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3305,"bookHadithIndex":55,"text":"It was narrated from Abu Darda’ that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The best food of the people of this world and the people of Paradise is meat.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3305-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3305-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3305-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3305-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced2","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3306,"bookHadithIndex":56,"text":"It was narrated that Abu Darda’ said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was never invited to eat meat but he would respond, and he was never offered meat as a gift but he would accept it.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3306-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3306-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3306-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3306-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced3","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3307,"bookHadithIndex":57,"text":"It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:“One day some meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the foreleg was offered to him which he liked, so he bit it with his front teeth.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3307-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3307-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3307-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3307-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced4","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3308,"bookHadithIndex":58,"text":"‘Abdullah bin Ja’far told Ibn Zubair, who had slaughtered a camel for them, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he (‘Abdullah) said:“Some people were bringing meat to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: ‘The best meat is the meat of the back.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3308-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3308-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3308-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3308-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced5","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3309,"bookHadithIndex":59,"text":"It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“I do not know of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ever seeing a roasted sheep* until he met Allah.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3309-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3309-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3309-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3309-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced6","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3310,"bookHadithIndex":60,"text":"It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“No leftovers of roast meat* were ever cleared from in front of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and no carpet was ever carried with him.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3310-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3310-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3310-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3310-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced7","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3311,"bookHadithIndex":61,"text":"It was narrated that ‘Abdullah bin Harith bin Jaz’ Az-Zubaidi said:“We ate food with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the mosque, meat that had been roasted. Then we wiped our hands on the pebbles and got up to perform prayer without performing ablution.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3311-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3311-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3311-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3311-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced8","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3312,"bookHadithIndex":62,"text":"It was narrated that Abu Mas`ud said:“A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and his voice trembled out of awe as he spoke to him. The Prophet said to him, “Be calm, for I am not a king. Verily, I am only the son of a woman who ate dried meat.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3312-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3312-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3312-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ced9","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3313,"bookHadithIndex":63,"text":"It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“We used to store trotters and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would eat them fifteen days after the sacrifice.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3313-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3313-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3313-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3313-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ceda","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3314,"bookHadithIndex":64,"text":"It was narrated from ‘Abdullah bin ‘Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Two kinds of dead meat and two kinds of blood have been permitted to us. The two kinds of dead meat are fish and locusts, and the two kinds of blood are the liver and spleen.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3314-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3314-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3314-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3314-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cedb","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3315,"bookHadithIndex":65,"text":"It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:‘The best of your seasonings is salt.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3315-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3315-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3315-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3315-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cedc","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3316,"bookHadithIndex":66,"text":"It was narrated from ‘Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“What a blessed condiment vinegar is.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3316-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3316-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3316-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3316-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cedd","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3317,"bookHadithIndex":67,"text":"It was narrated from Jabir bin ‘Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“What a blessed condiment vinegar is.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3317-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3317-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3317-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cede","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3318,"bookHadithIndex":68,"text":"Umm Sa’d said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon ‘Aishah, when I was with her, and said: ‘Is there any food?’ She said: ‘We have bread, dates and vinegar.’ The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘What a blessed condiment vinegar is. O Allah, bless vinegar, for it was the condiment of the Prophets before me, and no house will ever be poor in which there is vinegar.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3318-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Mawdu"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3318-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Mawdu"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3318-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Mawdu"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3318-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cedf","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3319,"bookHadithIndex":69,"text":"It was narrated from ‘Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:‘Season (your food) with olive oil and anoint yourselves with it, for it comes from a blessed tree.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3319-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3319-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3319-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee0","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3320,"bookHadithIndex":70,"text":"‘Abdullah bin Sa’eed narrated that his grandfather said:“I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘Eat (olive) oil and anoint yourselves with it, for it is blessed.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3320-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3320-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3320-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3320-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee1","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3321,"bookHadithIndex":71,"text":"I heard ‘Aishah say:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would say, when milk was brought to him: ‘A blessing,’ or ‘Two blessings.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3321-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3321-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3321-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3321-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee2","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3322,"bookHadithIndex":72,"text":"It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever is given food by Allah, let him say: Allahumma barik lana fihi wa arzuqna khairan minhu (O Allah, bless it for us and provide us with something better than it). And whoever is given milk to drink by Allah, let him say: Allahumma barik lana fihi wa zidna minhu (O Allah, bless it for us and give us more of it). For I do not know of any food or drink that suffices, apart from milk.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3322-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3322-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3322-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3322-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee3","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3323,"bookHadithIndex":73,"text":"(It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“The Messenger of Allah 9saw) used to like sweets and honey.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3323-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3323-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3323-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3323-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee4","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3324,"bookHadithIndex":74,"text":"It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“My mother was trying to fatten me up when she wanted to send me to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (when she got married), but nothing worked until I ate cucumbers with dates; then I grew plump like the best kind of plump.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3324-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3324-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3324-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee5","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3325,"bookHadithIndex":75,"text":"It was narrated ‘Abdullah bin Ja’far said:“I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) eating cucumbers with dates.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3325-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3325-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3325-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3325-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee6","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3326,"bookHadithIndex":76,"text":"It was narrated that Sahl bin Sa’d said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to eat dates with melon.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3326-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3326-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3326-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3326-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee7","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3327,"bookHadithIndex":77,"text":"It was narrated from ‘Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“A house in which there are no dates, its people will go hungry.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3327-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3327-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3327-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3327-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee8","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3328,"bookHadithIndex":78,"text":"It was narrated from ‘Ubaidullah bin Abu Rafi’, from his grandmother Salma, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“A house in which there are no dates is like a house in which there is no food.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3328-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3328-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3328-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih Lighairihi"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3328-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cee9","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3329,"bookHadithIndex":79,"text":"It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that when the first fruits (of the season) were brought, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would say:“O Allah, bless us in our city and in our fruits, in our Mudd and in our Sa’,* blessing upon blessing.” Then he would give it to the smallest of the children present","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3329-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3329-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3329-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3329-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ceea","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3330,"bookHadithIndex":80,"text":"It was narrated from ‘Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Eat unripe dates with ripe one and eat old dates with new ones, for Satan gets angry and says: ‘The son of Adam will survive so long as he eats old dates with new ones.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3330-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Mawdu"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3330-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Mawdu"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3330-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3330-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ceeb","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3331,"bookHadithIndex":81,"text":"Ibn ‘Umar said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade eating two dates at once unless he asks his companions permission to do so.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3331-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3331-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3331-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3331-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ceec","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3332,"bookHadithIndex":82,"text":"It was narrated from Sa’d, the freed slave of Abu Bakr – and Sa’d used to serve the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he liked this Hadith – that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade eating two dates at once","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3332-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3332-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3332-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih Lighairihi"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3332-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ceed","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3333,"bookHadithIndex":83,"text":"It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he was brought some old dates; he started to inspect them.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3333-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3333-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3333-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3333-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ceee","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3334,"bookHadithIndex":84,"text":"It was narrated that the two sons of Busr, who were of the tribe of Sulaim, said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon us. We placed a velvet cloth of ours beneath him and sprinkled water on it.* He sat on it, and Allah sent down Revelation to him in our house. We offered him butter and dates, and he (ﷺ) liked butter.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3334-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3334-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3334-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ceef","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3335,"bookHadithIndex":85,"text":"‘Abdul-‘Aziz bin Abu Hazim said:My father told me: I asked Sahl bin Sa’d: “Did you ever see dough made from well-sifted flour?” He said: “I never saw dough made from well-sifted flour until the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed away.” I said: “Did they have sieves at the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?” He said: “I never saw a sieve until the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed away.” I said: “How did you eat barley that was not sifted?” He said: “We used to blow on it, and whatever flew away, flew away, and whatever was left we made dough with it.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3335-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3335-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3335-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3335-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih Sahih Bukhari"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef0","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3336,"bookHadithIndex":86,"text":"It was narrated from Umm Ayman that she sifted some flour and made a loaf of bread for the Prophet (ﷺ). He said:“What is this?” She said: “It is food that we make in our land, and I wanted to make a loaf of it for you. He said: “Fold it onto itself and knead it.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3336-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3336-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Hasan Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3336-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3336-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef1","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3337,"bookHadithIndex":87,"text":"It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never saw a thin loaf made from well-sifted flour with his own eyes, until he met Allah.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3337-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3337-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3337-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3337-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef2","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3338,"bookHadithIndex":88,"text":"It was narrated from Ibn ‘Ata that his father said:“Abu Hurairah visited his people, meaning, a village” – I (one of the narrators) think he said: “Yuna” – “And they brought him some of the first thin loaves of bread. He wept and said: ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never saw such a thing with his own eyes.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3338-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3338-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3338-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3338-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef3","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3339,"bookHadithIndex":89,"text":"Qatadah said:“We used to go to (visit) Anas bin Malik.” (One of the narrators) Ishaq said: “And his baker was standing there.” (In another narration) Darimi said: “And his table was set. He said one day: ‘(Come and) eat, for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never saw any thin loaf of bread until he met Allah, nor any roasted sheep (with skin).’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3339-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3339-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3339-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3339-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef4","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3340,"bookHadithIndex":90,"text":"It was narrated that Ibn ‘Abbas said:“The first we heard of Faludhaj* was when Jibril (as) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ‘The world will be opened for your nation and they will conquer the world, until they eat Faludhaj.’ The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ‘What is Faludhaj?’ He said: ‘They mix ghee and honey together.’ At that, the Prophet (ﷺ) sobbed.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3340-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Mawdu"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3340-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Munkar"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3340-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Mawdu"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3340-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef5","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3341,"bookHadithIndex":91,"text":"It was narrated that Ibn ‘Umar said:“One day, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘I wish that we had some white bread made of brown wheat, softened with ghee, that we could eat.’ A man from among the Ansar heard that, so he took some (of that food) and brought it to him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘Where was this ghee kept?’ He said: ‘In a container made of mastigure skin.’ And he refused to eat it.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3341-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3341-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3341-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3341-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef6","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3342,"bookHadithIndex":92,"text":"It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“Umm Sulaim made some bread for the Prophet (ﷺ), and she put a little ghee on it. Then she said: ‘Go to the Prophet (ﷺ) and invite him (to come and eat).’ So I went and told him: ‘My mother is inviting you (to come and eat).’ So he stood up, and said to the people who were with him: ‘Get up.’ I went ahead of him and told her. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) came and said: ‘Bring what you have made.’ She said: ‘I only made it for you alone.’ He said: ‘Bring it.’ Then he said: ‘O Anas, bring (them) in to me ten by ten.’ So I kept bringing them in ten by ten, and they ate their fill, and there were eighty of them.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3342-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3342-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3342-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef7","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3343,"bookHadithIndex":93,"text":"It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:“By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) never ate his fill of wheat bread for three days in a row, until Allah took his soul.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3343-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3343-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3343-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3343-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef8","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3344,"bookHadithIndex":94,"text":"it was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“The family of Muhammad (ﷺ) never ate their fill of wheat bread for three nights in a row, from the time they came to Al-Madinah until he passed away.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3344-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3344-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3344-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3344-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cef9","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3345,"bookHadithIndex":95,"text":"It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“When the Prophet (ﷺ) passed away, there was nothing in my house that any living soul could eat, except a little bit of barley on a shelf of mine. I ate it for a long time, then I weighed it and soon it was all gone.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3345-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3345-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3345-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3345-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cefa","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3346,"bookHadithIndex":96,"text":"It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“The family of Muhammad (ﷺ) never ate their fill of barley bread until he was taken (i.e. died).”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3346-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3346-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3346-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3346-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cefb","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3347,"bookHadithIndex":97,"text":"It was narrated that Ibn ‘Abbas said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to spend many nights in a row hungry and his family could find no supper, and usually their bread was barley bread.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3347-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3347-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3347-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3347-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cefc","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3348,"bookHadithIndex":98,"text":"It was narrated from Hasan that Anas bin Malik said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wore wool, and his shows were sandals.”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3348-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3348-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3348-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Very Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3348-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cefd","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3349,"bookHadithIndex":99,"text":"Miqdam bin Madikarib said:“I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ‘A human being fills no worse vessel than his stomach. It is sufficient for a human being to eat a few mouthfuls to keep his spine straight. But if he must (fill it), then one third of food, one third for drink and one third for air.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3349-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3349-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3349-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3349-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cefe","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324","bookIndex":29,"hadithIndex":3350,"bookHadithIndex":100,"text":"It was narrated that Ibn ‘Umar said:“A man burped in the presence of the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: ‘Withhold your burps from us! For the most hungry of you on the Day of Resurrection will be those who most ate their fill in this world.’”","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3350-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3350-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi","name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3350-shuaibalarnaut","name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sanad Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3350-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]}]}